# Lean process redesign — tighten-sdd-artifact-boundaries

## Current work

User authorized implementation on 2026-11-03 after specifying the new process.
Flow: short proposal with work items → unchanged-format requirements → external
interface and item skeleton in system → item design/review/code/review.
Proposal holds work items; the main agent prepares initial artifacts and
coordinates their executors. Special check sections in system require an
explicit user request; implementation receives appropriate checks.
Minor earlier corrections are autonomous; significant
inconsistencies require the user's decision.

Participation: involved, batch review of the completed change after code.
No commits unless requested; do not archive before the user reviews the result.

## Verification after user review

On 2026-11-03 the user ended remarks and explicitly requested checks.
The original executors verified their updated sources and fixed defects.
Tests, validators, independent reviews, builds and bootstrap reinstallation
completed; current evidence follows. Historical evidence is labelled separately.

Comment 1: `system ↔ implementation` means that architecture and code develop
together. Proposal and requirements may also be revisited when necessary.
The English/Russian rules, schema, packaged skills, project guidance and affected
change contracts are being aligned. Installed local skills will be refreshed
through specd-bootstrap when review ends.

Comment 2: restore detailed responsibility and abstraction-level boundaries
for requirements, system and ADRs from the earlier rules, retaining concise
generated architecture. Describe existing owners and contracts directly;
remove descriptions of absent entities and historical contrasts from current
model prose. Keep legitimate imposed constraints and meaningful owner boundaries.

Comment 3 concerns the Requirements section of rules.md, not the change's
requirements delta. Preserve its previously satisfactory content, ordering and
scenario presentation; adjust owner references only where the current model
requires it. The original artifact executor applies that restoration in EN/RU.

Comment 4: creation of an ADR requires the user's explicit request. Existing
decision history is preserved. The unrequested ADR draft in this change has
been removed; reconcile the optional artifact state when lifecycle work resumes.

Comment 5: rules EN/RU use descriptive/declarative artifact-model prose.
The original executor changes grammatical voice while preserving the detailed
boundaries, examples, content and earlier accepted corrections. Operational
schema and skill instructions keep the form appropriate to their purpose.

Comment 6: the System section presents suitable and unsuitable descriptions as
two explicit example lists with brief explanations. Existing illustrative prose
is reorganized; detailed ownership and abstraction-level boundaries remain.

Comment 7: System authoring instructions in the schema carry the example lists,
including conventional CLI usage, idiomatic Rust Result and descriptions of
absent process stages as unsuitable architecture content. The process System
describes expanding these examples as a way to refine author/reviewer criteria
and prevent recurring poor content choices. The original Artifacts executor
owns both source edits.

During these edits, installed schema files inherited read-only Nix-store modes
through bootstrap's fs::copy. The artifact owner makes its workspace files
writable to continue editing. Delivery now owns a minimal installer correction
and regression checks for writable installed resources.

## Original executors

| Item | Executor | Owned implementation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Artifacts | `/root/artifacts` | schema, templates, rules EN/RU; system Artifacts section |
| 2. Agents | `/root/agents` | local and packaged skills; system Agents section |
| 3. Delivery | `/root/delivery` | bootstrap VM test, project context; system Delivery section |

Keep these original sessions resumable through user review. Route questions
and corrections to the corresponding executor; the orchestrator does not take
over those edits or assign a replacement. Report an unavailable original session.
The main session owns proposal, requirements and the shared external interface.
Independent design reviewer `/root/design_review` passed the three scoped designs.
Separate code reviewer `/root/code_review` passed the implemented sources and
rechecked corrections made by their original executors before this review.
User comments are incorporated. The same independent code reviewer passed all
three source scopes, including Delivery's permission correction, and approved
the final integration after build, VM and canonical-install evidence.

## Post-review evidence

- Current schema validates: four artifacts, five workflow steps, no warnings.
  Disposable real-CLI lifecycle and emitted-instruction probes passed:
  `/tmp/lean-sdd-artifacts-final-5eg0gx3e/probe-results.json` and
  `emission-results.json`. The System instruction carries six good and eight
  bad examples with the agreed qualifications.
- All 24 packaged skill entries, 108 links, resource reachability and native
  syntax parity passed: `/tmp/specd-agents-validation.json`.
- Root reread the merged requirements/system and validated proposal and
  requirements. Optional ADR is explicitly skipped because none was requested.
  Redundant heading lines were removed from modified requirement delta bodies;
  merged heading ownership and contract meaning remain unchanged.
- Fixed bootstrap regular-file copies to add owner-write while preserving
  other permission bits. All 11 Rust unit tests passed, including installation
  and update from read-only resources with preserved executability.
  Package: `/nix/store/d4lwg4hp2amgnmfhlq6cm5brvzqsj6f6-specd-bootstrap-0.1.0`.
  Build log: `/nix/store/72bpqipjq8hldavlqzfb0g4q1058jgv8-specd-bootstrap-0.1.0.drv`.
- Full bootstrap VM passed with `checkOpenCodeDiscovery = false`:
  `/nix/store/212xshmbrpl017c1nkjc8kx4q8x78k2h-vm-test-run-specd-bootstrap`.
  Driver type/lint checks passed. No OpenCode/KiloCode client was launched.
- Refreshed canonical Codex through the newly built `specd-bootstrap`.
  All 18 files match the packaged tree, eight local skills validate, 36 local
  links resolve, and all 36 installed paths have correct ownership and writable
  owner modes: `/tmp/specd-agents-canonical-validation.json`.
- Final lifecycle reached `archivable`: required artifacts complete, optional
  ADR skipped, no blockers or drift. No commits or archive performed.

## Historical pre-review evidence

Before user review, lifecycle reached `archivable` with all four artifacts
complete and no blockers or drift. Current review edits have not been validated.
The change has not been archived or committed.

- Schema validation and disposable real-CLI probes passed: partial system permits
  coding, proposal marks preserve validation, final tasks gate closure, no-op
  requirements/system work for a covered fix. Probe index:
  `/tmp/lean-sdd-artifacts-final-5x3nx638/probe-results.json`.
- All 24 packaged skill entries passed the skill validator; resource links,
  native invocation syntax and CLI command examples were checked. Each tree
  shrank from 3,085 to 632 lines.
- Built bootstrap: `/nix/store/lrsqsx3ppw4gl3064lqj59iz0694c3l0-specd-bootstrap-0.1.0`.
  Installed local Codex resources through `nix run .#specd-bootstrap -- --target
  <project-root> --agent codex`; local/package trees match exactly. No manual
  skill copy succeeded or is needed.
- Full bootstrap VM test passed after the original Delivery executor repaired
  fixture-local Git identity and relocated syntax assertions. Result:
  `/nix/store/h5sfdbh9prckcmqw2jl3ypvksr26i0nl-vm-test-run-specd-bootstrap`.
  Used `checkOpenCodeDiscovery = false`; OpenCode and KiloCode clients were not
  launched. Their resource installation/update was checked as files only.

The verified change is ready for closure. Forward further questions or
corrections to the original executors above.

